\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Off-policy replay condition}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{replay}
\tag{off-policy}

\p{At update attempt #{n}, let #{\nu_n} be the policy stamp of the current
executable action policy. A replay attempt satisfies a \strong{bounded-ratio
condition} with constant #{R\geq1} if every active action in the attempted
update obeys}

##{
  R^{-1}\leq
  \frac{\pi^{\nu_n}(A_t\mid H_t)}{\pi^{\nu_b}(A_t\mid H_t)}
  \leq R.
}

\p{This is a standard off-policy regularity condition expressed with the PPO
likelihood ratio \citef{schulman2017proximal}. It implies shared support on the
active samples. It does not control unvisited histories or the environment
state distribution.}

\p{Dynamic Gradient Gating \citef{miao2026when} uses a head-gradient alarm
rather than this hard condition. A later theorem should distinguish a direct
ratio assumption from an empirical diagnostic that may correlate with it.}
